   "id": 471362,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A research study is being conducted to understand the opinions of people on the new city budget. The population consists of residents from different neighborhoods in the city with varying income levels. The following table provides the data of 130 participants randomly selected for the study, categorized by their neighborhood and income level.\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table id=\"tab2\">\n<tbody><tr><th>\n</th></tr><tr>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>Neighborhood</strong></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>Income Level</strong></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><strong>Number of Participants</strong></td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody><tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Northside</td>\n<td>Low Income</td>\n<td align=\"center\">35</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Southside</td>\n<td>Middle Income</td>\n<td align=\"center\">50</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Eastside</td>\n<td>High Income</td>\n<td align=\"center\">45</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n<caption>Neighborhood and Income level Category</caption>\n</table>\nWhat sampling technique was used to collect this data? \n",
